{"sessionId":"01a131be-1d0d-7243-8af8-b49428b78080","update":{"availableCommands":[{"description":"Report a bug — opens GitHub issue form","input":{"hint":"Provide a concise title (3-5 words) to describe the issue."},"name":"bug"},{"description":"Connect to and query the ai-optimizer ClickHouse instance in prod-master.\nManages port-forwarding automatically, runs queries via the HTTP interface,\nand can explore databases and tables. Use when querying ai-optimizer analytics\ndata (chat_completions, requests, audit_events, feedbacks, etc.).","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:aioptimizer-ch"},{"description":"Analyze and understand in detail the results of a benchmark run.\nUse when the user asks to inspect, debug, or compare a benchmark run —\nincluding pass rates, failure modes, agent timeouts, token usage, costs,\ninference speed, error categories, and per-task verdicts.\nCovers: fetching artifacts from GCS, finding scheduled pipeline runs,\nand querying the ML ClickHouse table (dwh.kimchi_benchmark_runs).","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:analyze-benchmark-run"},{"description":"Use for \"automate me\", \"create/update/refresh my -mode skill\", \"turn/capture my preferences or working style into a skill\", or wanting agents to follow how the user works. Drafts or revises a personal -mode skill via create-skill + unslop, optionally pulling fresh evidence from recent transcripts.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:automate-me"},{"description":"Launch or schedule benchmark pipelines (Terminal Bench 2.x, SWE-bench Pro, DeepSWE) in castai/kimchi/kimchi. Covers one-off runs via glab ci run, pipeline schedule create/update/list with correctly typed CI inputs, and the CI input contract. Default dataset is TB 2.1.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:benchmark-pipelines"},{"description":"Find what a change could break somewhere else before it ships, beyond the diff, and prove the one fact it's safe because of by running real code instead of writing it up. Use for 'blast radius of X', 'what could this break', or reviewing a small diff you don't trust.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:blast-radius"},{"description":"Account and customer intelligence for CAST AI via the SA MCP server. Use to research an account, prep for a call or QBR, review a deal or POC, assess account health, churn or renewal risk, qualify technical fit, find or enrich contacts, prep outreach, or search internal knowledge (Confluence, GitHub, Slack, Gong, Jira). Triggers on a company name, domain, CAST org UUID, or Apollo org ID paired with any research, status, health, or outreach question — e.g. \"tell me about Acme\", \"get me Walgreens account health\", \"status of the Contoso POC\", \"is Globex at risk?\", \"who should I email at X?\", \"QBR prep\", \"meeting prep\", \"what did we say about pricing?\", \"dig deeper into these orgs\", \"T1 accounts to prioritize\". Also handles open-ended cross-source narrative questions — \"entire history of the Algolia deal\", \"why did we win/lose X\", \"sentiment arc across the calls\" — by delegating to the AMA research agent. The skill handles tool selection and ordering; users never name tools.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:cast-ai-sales-analyzer"},{"description":"Comprehensive CAST AI cluster optimization analysis. Combines six checks into one skill: (1) Evictor log parsing to find nodes blocked from consolidation, (2) Pod health scan for Pending/Failed/CrashLoopBackOff pods, (3) Max-pod-per-node analysis showing each node configuration's pod limit and flagging nodes running at capacity, (4) Node template analysis identifying redundant templates and consolidation opportunities based on arch, capacity type, OS, and taints, (5) Node template CPU:Memory ratio profiling to recommend memory-heavy, compute-heavy, or general-purpose instance families plus a DaemonSet overhead advisory for large clusters, (6) WOOP rollout strategy audit checking for one-by-one rollout and zero-downtime enforcement on single-replica workloads.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:cluster-optimization-analysis"},{"description":"CAST AI TAM tool: run a full CAST AI readiness assessment and generate branded PDF reports for any cluster or org. Trigger on: \"readiness check\", \"onboarding assessment\", \"safe to enable evictor\", \"ready to enable cast ai\", \"pre-prod check\", \"cluster health report\", \"anti-pattern scan\", \"check all clusters\", or when a cluster ID / org ID is passed with questions about enabling automation. Also trigger on \"run the checklist\", \"generate the report\", or \"assess this cluster / all clusters\".\nAccept input in any of these forms:\n  - A bare cluster UUID  → single-cluster report\n  - A console URL containing a cluster ID → single-cluster report\n  - An org ID (e.g. bebc00d7-...)  → org-wide: list clusters, confirm scope, run all\n  - An account name (e.g. \"run for Contoso\") → resolve via Pylon, confirm cluster(s)\n  - \"all clusters\" with an org ID  → org-wide run across every cluster","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:cluster-readiness"},{"description":"Review the changes since a fixed point (commit, branch, tag, or merge-base) along two axes — Standards (does the code follow this repo's documented coding standards?) and Spec (does the code match what the originating issue/spec asked for?). Runs both reviews in parallel sub-agents and reports them side by side. Use when the user wants to review a branch, a PR, work-in-progress changes, or asks to \"review since X\".","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:code-review"},{"description":"Guide authoring of dense, narrative-driven Confluence documents capped at 7 minutes reading time (~1,750 words of prose). Trigger whenever someone is writing, drafting, or co-authoring a Confluence page, proposal, design doc, analysis, strategy doc, or any internal write-up. Also trigger when someone asks to \"write a doc\", \"draft a page\", \"help me write up\", \"write a proposal\", or shares a draft for review/editing. Trigger for any task where the output is an internal document. Do NOT trigger for external content (blog posts, case studies, customer docs) or postmortems (use rca-review skill).","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:confluence-author"},{"description":"Build or adapt a local harness to drive, inspect, and profile an interactive CLI or TUI without external services. Use for CLI UX checks, startup regressions, memory leaks, hangs, prompt flows, or terminal demos.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:control-cli"},{"description":"Build or adapt a local browser/CDP harness to drive and inspect a web, IDE, or Electron UI. Use for local UI verification, screenshots, accessibility snapshots, perf profiles, visual diffs, or reproducing UI bugs.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:control-ui"},{"description":"Create or update reusable skills from a task or workflow.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:create-skill"},{"description":"Generate a project-local verification skill that drives your app the way a user does — any language, framework, or platform. Use for /create-verification-skill, \"make a control skill for this repo\", or when a project has no scripted way to prove UI/CLI/service behavior.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:create-verification-skill"},{"description":"Diagnose runtime state with persistent DAP debugger sessions — breakpoints, expression eval, and stepping across Go, Python, TypeScript/JavaScript, and native binaries","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:dap-debugging"},{"description":"Use when running ClickHouse or PostgreSQL queries, exploring schemas, or accessing database data in this project. Use instead of raw CLI tools or direct port connections.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:db-utility"},{"description":"Diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions. Use when the user says \"diagnose\"/\"debug this\", or reports something broken/throwing/failing/slow.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:diagnosing-bugs"},{"description":"Search and read Discord messages, channels, and DMs via the Discord API using a\nuser auth token. Use when the user asks to find or search Discord messages,\nlook up Discord conversations, check a Discord channel or thread, find a\nDiscord user ID, or reference something discussed on Discord.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:discord-search"},{"description":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to create, read, edit, or manipulate Word documents (.docx) or Word templates (.dotx). Triggers include: any mention of Microsoft Word Documents, such as 'Word doc', 'word document', '.docx', '.dotx', 'microsoft doc'. Also use when extracting or reorganizing content from .docx or .dotx files, inserting or replacing images in documents, find-and-replace in Word files, working with tracked changes or comments, or converting content into a polished Word document. If the user asks for a deliverable as a Word or .docx file (to download, email or print), use this skill. However, if they ask for a document, page, report, memo, or notes WITHOUT naming a file format and the session offers Claude's own dedicated document or page skill or connector, use that instead, even if they will email or print it. Do NOT use for PDFs, spreadsheets, Google Docs, or coding unrelated to document generation.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:docx"},{"description":"Analyze essays, proposals, memos, specifications, policies, research papers, strategy documents, and other arguments using stickman, steelman, strawman, and first-principles reasoning. Use when asked to review a document rigorously, reconstruct its argument, expose assumptions, make the strongest case for it, anticipate uncharitable readings, critique it fairly, or determine what conclusions survive scrutiny.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:first-principles-document-review"},{"description":"Read this before the first Google Drive, Docs, Sheets or Slides connector call whenever the task creates or changes a Google file. Use this skill whenever the user wants to create or change a Google Doc, Sheet or Slides file in their Google Drive. Triggers include: a request that names Google Docs, Sheets, Slides or Drive and asks to make, edit, format, copy or rename a file; a docs.google.com link with a request to change that file, even a one-line fix or suggested edits; and any follow-up change to a Google file from earlier in the chat, even \"change it\" or \"add a tab\". Includes helper scripts for document positions, cell ranges and slide layout. However, if the user asks for a doc, deck or spreadsheet without naming Google, or gives a Google file only as source material for something new, use Claude's own output type instead. Do NOT use for read-only questions about a Google file, or for Word, Excel, PowerPoint or PDF files.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:google-workspace"},{"description":"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:grill-me"},{"description":"A relentless interview to sharpen a plan or design, which also creates docs (ADR's and glossary) as we go.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:grill-with-docs"},{"description":"Compact the current conversation into a handoff document for another agent to pick up.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:handoff"},{"description":"Import a memory export from another AI assistant into Claude's memory — conversationally, additively, and with the content treated as data.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:import-memory"},{"description":"Run the curator — consolidate the agent-created skill library via umbrella-building","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:improve"},{"description":"Debug inference issues in a kimchi session or model deployment — hung/stalled\nrequests, high latency, empty streams, provider errors, 499s, runaway generations.\nTraces a request end-to-end: kimchi harness → ai-optimizer-proxy → litellm\nsidecar → sgl-model-gateway (smg) → sglang engines on Omni/Nebius.\nCovers: ai-optimizer ClickHouse (chat_completions), Loki (proxy + router logs),\nVictoriaLogs (sglang engine logs), cast-prometheus (sglang_* metrics), and the\nopinionated queries and pitfalls for each.\nOut of scope: fetching benchmark results/artifacts — use analyze-benchmark-run.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:investigate-inference"},{"description":"Work the way jose expects — surgical diffs, evidence-backed verification, structured delegation, and a strict delivery loop ending in draft PRs. Use on \"/jose-mode\" or when asked to work in jose's style.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:jose-mode"},{"description":"Control Kimchi TUI through tmux.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:kimchi-tmux"},{"description":"Fetch and analyze logs from CAST AI Loki (prod-master, prod-eu) via kubectl port-forward with an IAP fallback. Runs arbitrary LogQL queries against any service/namespace, and ships a ready-made \"apa-errors\" preset for APA production error debugging. Use whenever searching logs, checking errors/panics, or debugging a service in a CAST AI environment.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:loki-logs"},{"description":"Periodic pass that keeps a project's verification skill and feature map honest: parallel source readers per feature, one live session driving every feature, at most one PR of proven corrections. Use for /maintain-verification-skill or \"audit the verify skill\".","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:maintain-verification-skill"},{"description":"Connect to and query the ML ClickHouse cluster in prod-master.\nManages port-forwarding automatically, runs queries via the HTTP interface,\nand can explore databases and tables. Use when querying ML benchmark data\n(dwh.kimchi_benchmark_runs, etc.).","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:ml-ch"},{"description":"Render the user's morning brief as a styled HTML artifact, or set it up as a recurring weekday task. Use only when the user explicitly asks to run, see, or set up their morning brief, or if they invoke /morning by name. A question about their day, schedule, or calendar is not by itself a request for the brief; answer it directly instead.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:morning"},{"description":"Resolve organization IDs to names (or names to IDs) using the Kubecast Billing API in prod-master. Look up by UUID to get the org name, or search by name to get the UUID.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:org-lookup"},{"description":"Use this skill whenever the user wants to do anything with PDF files. This includes reading or extracting text/tables from PDFs, combining or merging multiple PDFs into one, splitting PDFs apart, rotating pages, adding watermarks, creating new PDFs, filling PDF forms, encrypting/decrypting PDFs, extracting images, and OCR on scanned PDFs to make them searchable. If the user mentions a .pdf file or asks to produce one, use this skill.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:pdf"},{"description":"Gather interactions with a colleague across Discord, Jira, and Confluence to\nprepare structured peer feedback. Finds DMs, shared channels/threads,\nsubstantial messages, Jira tickets where both participated, and Confluence\npages authored, summarizes them, interviews the user for additional data\npoints, and produces a feedback document answering:\nwhat is this person doing well, and how could they improve their collaboration?","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:peer-feedback"},{"description":"Multi-persona review skill for writeups, product docs, design docs, RFCs, ADRs, implementation plans, feature specs, release notes, and proposals. Generates feedback from 9 perspectives: CTO/VP Engineering, Principal Engineer, Product Manager, Sales Engineer, Solutions Architect, QA Engineer, Sales, Customer Support, and Customer (end-user). Use this skill whenever someone asks to \"review as different personas\", \"get multi-perspective feedback\", \"persona review\", \"stakeholder review\", or wants a document evaluated through multiple professional lenses. ALSO trigger when someone writes or shares product documentation, technical design docs, RFCs, or big implementation/architecture changes — these always benefit from multi-persona review even without explicit ask. Trigger for partial requests like \"what would sales think\" or \"how would an engineer see this\" — run the full panel unless told to limit it.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:persona-review"},{"description":"Query the ai-optimizer catalog PostgreSQL (models/deprecations, providers, rate limits, etc. in prod-master) read-only through the observatorium Grafana postgres datasource. Use when inspecting the kubecast models catalog: model deprecation/sunset records, replacements and alternatives, providers metadata, or any other table in that database — especially when direct Postgres access is blocked (Cloud SQL private IP, restricted creds).","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:postgresql-ai"},{"description":"Use this skill any time a .pptx or .potx file is involved in any way — as input, output, or both. This includes: creating slide decks, pitch decks, or presentations as PowerPoint (.pptx) files; reading, parsing, or extracting text from any .pptx or .potx file (even if the extracted content will be used elsewhere, like in an email, summary, or creating a different type of slide deck); editing, modifying, or updating existing presentations; combining or splitting slide files; working with templates (.potx), layouts, speaker notes, or comments. Trigger whenever the user asks for a PowerPoint or .pptx file, or references a .pptx or .potx filename, regardless of what they plan to do with the content afterward. However, when the user asks for a deck, slides, a slide deck, or a presentation without naming a file format, default to using a dedicated slide-deck artifact type or a separate slides skill if this session offers one; otherwise, use this skill.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:pptx"},{"description":"Apply to any non-trivial work, not just bulk work: edits, migrations, analyses, checks. Build the tool that does it or proves it (codemod, script, generator, or a skill your subagents follow) instead of working by hand. The tool is the artifact a reviewer can rerun.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:principle-build-the-lever"},{"description":"Apply when you catch yourself writing the same instruction a second time, or notice a recurring correction. Encode the rule as a lint, metadata flag, runtime check, or script instead of more text.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:principle-encode-lessons-in-structure"},{"description":"Apply when refactoring, evaluating diff size, or tempted to add abstractions, layers, or signal threading. Bias toward deletion and the smallest change that solves the problem.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:principle-laziness-protocol"},{"description":"Apply after completing a task, before declaring done. Verify against the real artifact (run the feature, read the actual value, inspect the diff), not a proxy, self-report, or 'it compiles.'","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:principle-prove-it-works"},{"description":"Apply to multi-step work (sweeps, migrations, runs of similar edits) and to how you stack commits and PRs. Break work into small units that each end in a verifiable state, check each before the next, and order delivery so the sequence proves itself to a reviewer.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:principle-sequence-verifiable-units"},{"description":"Review, critique, and improve production incident RCA (Root Cause Analysis) and postmortem documents for CAST AI infrastructure systems (Kubernetes, autoscaling, operators, control planes, cloud cost optimization). Use this skill whenever someone asks to review an RCA, review a postmortem, check incident write-up quality, evaluate 5-Whys analysis, assess action items from an incident, help write or improve an RCA document, or mentions \"RCA\", \"postmortem\", \"incident review\", \"root cause\", or \"production incident write-up\". Also trigger when someone pastes or uploads an incident document and asks for feedback, or when they share a Confluence page link containing an RCA. This skill covers both reviewing existing RCAs and helping author new ones from scratch.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:rca-review"},{"description":"CAST AI CP tool: generate a full ROI analysis PDF for a customer. Trigger on: \"ROI report\", \"generate savings report\", \"customer ROI\", \"calculate ROI\", \"savings analysis\", \"contract ROI\", or whenever an AE/TAM provides an org ID and ARR.\nRequired inputs (both must be provided in the command):\n  - ORG_ID:  the CAST AI organization UUID\n  - ARR:     the annual contract value (e.g. ARR: 17.136,00)\n\nExample usage:\n  /savings-roi-report ORG: dd0cd9d2-0c0d-4cf3-9e43-3e293a3e1271  ARR: 17.136,00","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:savings-roi-report"},{"description":"Keep a reviewable decision trail for long-running or unattended work: a TSV log with one row per decision (what, why, evidence, result). Local by default; commit it when a reviewer needs the trail to trust the result. Use for /show-me-your-work, autonomous or multi-phase runs, or work a human reviews after stepping away.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:show-me-your-work"},{"description":"Create new skills, modify and improve existing skills, and measure skill performance. Use when users want to create a skill from scratch, edit, or optimize an existing skill, run evals to test a skill, benchmark skill performance with variance analysis, or optimize a skill's description for better triggering accuracy.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:skill-creator"},{"description":"Interact with the Superset API at superset.prod-master.cast.ai — read and modify dashboards, charts, and datasets. Use when the user asks to read, update, or create Superset dashboards or charts.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:superset"},{"description":"Use only when the user explicitly asks for TDD, a failing test, or a regression test, OR when the bug has an obvious cheap local test target. Skip when the test path is unclear, expensive, integration-heavy, or not requested.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:tdd"},{"description":"Trace a single LLM request end-to-end through llm.cast.ai (Cloudflare → GCLB →\nnginx → ai-optimizer-proxy → litellm router sidecar → sgl-model-gateway →\nsglang/vLLM engines) to find which hop failed, stalled, or dropped it.\nUse when: correlating one request across ClickHouse/Loki/VictoriaLogs/Prometheus,\nmapping between session_id / trace_id / chatcmpl request_id, or quoting and\nre-verifying per-hop timeouts. For deep failure diagnosis (hangs, watchdog\nfires, spirals) use **investigate-inference**; for raw Loki access/LogQL use\n**loki-logs**; for ClickHouse connection details use **aioptimizer-ch**.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:trace-llm-request"},{"description":"Cut AI tells from any writing. Must always apply.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:unslop"},{"description":"Look up a Cast AI user by Auth0 identity ID (e.g. google-oauth2|..., auth0|...) or internal UUID, returning their name, email, and internal UUID. Uses the users service in prod-master via kubectl port-forward.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:user-lookup"},{"description":"Verify a claim with fresh local evidence: restate it falsifiably, capture baseline and treatment, compare artifacts, and return VERIFIED, NOT VERIFIED, or INCONCLUSIVE.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:verify-this"},{"description":"Connect to and query VictoriaTraces (distributed tracing backend, Jaeger-compatible API) across CAST AI environments. Covers the verified tailnet endpoint access, fetch-by-id and service-search recipes, span formats, sampling semantics, and the traps that make \"trace absent\" ambiguous. Use whenever fetching or analyzing distributed traces.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:victoriatraces"},{"description":"Writing documents for agents. Use when creating or editing skills, or modifying AGENTS.md or CLAUDE.md.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:writing-for-agents"},{"description":"Use this skill any time a spreadsheet file is the primary input or output. This means any task where the user wants to: open, read, edit, or fix an existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .xltx, .csv, or .tsv file (e.g., adding columns, computing formulas, formatting, charting, cleaning messy data); create a new spreadsheet from scratch or from other data sources; or convert between tabular file formats. Trigger especially when the user references a spreadsheet file by name or path — even casually (like \"the xlsx in my downloads\") — and wants something done to it or produced from it. Also trigger for cleaning or restructuring messy tabular data files (malformed rows, misplaced headers, junk data) into proper spreadsheets. The deliverable must be a spreadsheet file. Do NOT trigger when the primary deliverable is a Word document, HTML report, standalone Python script, database pipeline, or Google Sheets API integration, even if tabular data is involved.","input":{"hint":"Optional prompt to run with this skill loaded."},"name":"skill:xlsx"}],"sessionUpdate":"available_commands_update"}}
